-- title:
--   Descent of mathfrak m_Amathcal O_{X,x} along a base change
-- statement:
--   Let $A$ and $A_1$ be commutative local rings and $\iota_1 : A_1 \to A$ a local ring homomorphism whose composite with the residue map $A \to A/\mathfrak m_A$ is surjective. Let $X$, $X_1$ be schemes, $\mathrm{toBase} : X \to \operatorname{Spec} A$ and $f_1 : X_1 \to \operatorname{Spec} A_1$ morphisms, and let $e_1$ be an isomorphism from $X$ to the fibre product of $f_1$ and $\operatorname{Spec}(\iota_1)$ such that $e_1$ followed by the second projection is $\mathrm{toBase}$. Write $\pi$ for $e_1$ followed by the first projection, a morphism $X \to X_1$. Let $x$ be a point of $X$ whose image under $\mathrm{toBase}$ is the closed point of $\operatorname{Spec} A$, and let $r$ be an element of the stalk of $\mathcal O_{X_1}$ at $\pi(x)$. For a morphism $g : Y \to \operatorname{Spec} R$ and a point $y$ of $Y$, let $R \to \mathcal O_{Y,y}$ denote the composite of the canonical map $R \to \Gamma(\operatorname{Spec} R, \mathcal O)$, the map on global sections induced by $g$, and the germ map at $y$. The assertion is: if the image of $r$ under the stalk map of $\pi$ at $x$ lies in the ideal of $\mathcal O_{X,x}$ generated by the image of $\mathfrak m_A$ under $A \to \mathcal O_{X,x}$, then $r$ lies in the ideal of $\mathcal O_{X_1,\pi(x)}$ generated by the image of $\mathfrak m_{A_1}$ under $A_1 \to \mathcal O_{X_1,\pi(x)}$.
--
--   This is the statement that, at a point lying over the closed point, the ideal generated by the maximal ideal of the base contracts along the projection of a base change by a local homomorphism which is surjective onto the residue field; equivalently, $\mathcal O_{X_1,\pi(x)}/\mathfrak m_{A_1} \to \mathcal O_{X,x}/\mathfrak m_A$ is injective. It is used to descend a congruence modulo the maximal ideal from a scheme over $A$ to a scheme over the subring $A_1$, in [`AlgebraicCurve.SemistableModel.exists_eq_one_add_baseToFunctionField_mul_of_level`](thm.html#AlgebraicCurve.SemistableModel.exists_eq_one_add_baseToFunctionField_mul_of_level).
